  {"comment": "Joint's picks under another component than the active one (mitcad#1856, tools/ui-joint-holder-test.sh), like the reported design: Frame (Frame:1, O1, Sketch1 F1, Extrude1 F2: a 40 x 40 x 10 block at the origin, grounded) in the root, and Roller (Roller:1, O2, at x = 100), a sub-assembly of Shaft (Shaft:1, O3, F3/F4: a 20 x 20 x 20 block), Tube (Tube:1, O4, at x = 30 in Roller, F5/F6: the same block) and Collar (Collar:1, O5, at x = 60 in Roller, F7/F8: a 5 x 5 x 5 block), with a joint of its own (Tube onto Shaft, rigid, F9) and a rigid group (Shaft and Collar, F10). Carrier (Carrier:1, O6, at y = 100), a sub-assembly with a body of its own (F11/F12: a 20 x 20 x 20 block) and two parts, Pin (Pin:1, O6/O7, at x = 40 in Carrier, F13/F14) and Bush (Bush:1, O6/O8, at x = 80 in Carrier, F15/F16), the same block each, 20 apart so that the joint manipulator's ring on one pick does not cover the next (mitcad#2027: picks inside one sub-assembly with the root active). The blocks are 20 mm so that their top faces are wide enough to pick in the Windows test's view (a 1024 x 768 desktop with docked panels), where a 10 mm block's top face lay within its edges' pick reach. The root is active when the design opens. All geometry is synthetic."},
